<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ezana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 325–340 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as King Ezana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ezana was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksum</a> who reigned c. 325–340 CE. He converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, making the Aksumite Empire one of the first states to adopt the faith, and his coins and inscriptions reflect this change. His inscriptions also record a campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meroe">Meroë</a>, which is linked to the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ezana.jpg" alt="Ezana" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AXUM._Ezanas._Circa_330-360.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
